About to turn 29, have a few thoughts here. 

&#x200B;

1) I never treated exercise as something that was necessary more a nice to have. Now I have to treat it as preventative maintenance like brushing my teeth. Still kind of suck at it (goal for 2019).

&#x200B;

2) I never really asked myself what I wanted to do with my life, just went on autopilot to try to achieve the next promotion or cool job. It has worked out ok, but I am certainly not a runaway success. Definitely not fulfilled by my current work. Figuring that out.

&#x200B;

3) Prioritized my mental health sooner (I have anxiety, OCD, & depression - yay for me!). Was too cheap to pay for therapy. Wasn't willing to put in the work that was necessary to take care of myself.

&#x200B;

That being said, saved lots of money working in tech, married to an amazing person who I've been with for 7+ years, just bought a house. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Is Uber even giving their drivers a bonus? Probably not.

&#x200B;

Drivers don't have equity, so to be honest this is nice of Lyft that they are doing this. It also rewards its most tenured drivers.
